  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 335ac5b8367674445b672501b935617f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Page_02_Fire_Landslide
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CivilGame.Book.ManualPageData
  _leftPageTitle: 'THREAT: WILDFIRE'
  _leftPageIllustration: {fileID: 0}
  _leftPageContent: 'Another equally significant threat to fields and forests is the forest fire.



    It all begins with the appearance of a faint wisp of smoke above the treetops or the dry grass.



    Then, concentrated pockets of flame begin to form. Firefighters  shoud be called in second stage



    Eventually, this escalates into an uncontrollable blaze that consumes everything in its path.



    Preventive and responsive measures include calling in a lamberjacks to prevent fire in first ctage. And finaly rescue helicopter.  '
  _rightPageTitle: 'THREAT: LANDSLIDE'
  _rightPageIllustration: {fileID: 0}
  _rightPageContent: "While mountains may pose inherent risks, these dangers can sometimes be exacerbated by an earthquake occurring in the vicinity.\r\n\r\nLandslides often follow tremors\u2014which frequently happen at night\u2014and are typically accompanied by rocks falling from the slopes.\r\n\r\nThis is followed by a larger-scale collapse of rock formations, leading to the total destruction of the mountainside.\r\n\r\nTo prevent or minimize such damage, it is advisable to call in moountaineers in early stages. In critical stage you must call rescue helicopter. "
  _pageNumberText: 
